INSERT INTO public.interview_answers (id, "questionId", transcript, "durationSeconds", "timedOut", evaluation, "answeredAt", "correctedTranscript", "manuallyCorrected", "normalizedTranscript", "rawTranscript", "sttConfidence") VALUES ('cmuwf5x3g00d1wxxmvdfh10rg', 'cmuwf5srq00czwxxmiyn9orla', 'In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I led the development of a loan-application portal using the MERN stack. I was responsible for the entire architecture, starting with the React front-end, where I implemented the user interface using TypeScript and Redux Toolkit. This portal now supports around 120,000 customers monthly. On the backend, I designed REST APIs with Node.js and Express, incorporating JWT for secure authentication and role-based access. Additionally, I optimized our MongoDB performance, reducing query times by 60% through the use of compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This project not only improved user experience but also handled high traffic efficiently.', 48, false, '{"note": "The answer was strong but could benefit from more depth on challenges and solutions.", "relevance": 95, "needsFollowUp": true, "missingConcepts": ["challenges faced", "problem-solving strategies", "team collaboration"], "followUpQuestion": "Can you elaborate on any specific challenges you faced during the development process and how you overcame them?"}', '2026-10-01 06:49:32', NULL, false, 'In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I led the development of a loan-application portal using the MERN stack. I was responsible for the entire architecture, starting with the React front-end, where I implemented the user interface using TypeScript and Redux Toolkit. This portal now supports around 120,000 customers monthly. On the backend, I designed REST APIs with Node.js and Express.js, incorporating JWT for secure authentication and role-based access. Additionally, I optimized our MongoDB performance, reducing query times by 60% through the use of compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This project not only improved user experience but also handled high traffic efficiently.', 'In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I led the development of a loan-application portal using the MERN stack. I was responsible for the entire architecture, starting with the React front-end, where I implemented the user interface using TypeScript and Redux Toolkit. This portal now supports around 120,000 customers monthly. On the backend, I designed REST APIs with Node.js and Express, incorporating JWT for secure authentication and role-based access. Additionally, I optimized our MongoDB performance, reducing query times by 60% through the use of compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This project not only improved user experience but also handled high traffic efficiently.', 0.94);
INSERT INTO public.interview_answers (id, "questionId", transcript, "durationSeconds", "timedOut", evaluation, "answeredAt", "correctedTranscript", "manuallyCorrected", "normalizedTranscript", "rawTranscript", "sttConfidence") VALUES ('cmuwf61p800d5wxxmqca298qt', 'cmuwf5yhd00d3wxxm3qext5w5', 'Certainly! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, one major challenge was optimizing MongoDB query performance, as the application handled around 120,000 users monthly. Initial queries were slow, affecting user experience. To tackle this, I implemented compound indexes and utilized aggregation pipelines, which reduced query times by 60%. Additionally, I faced challenges with role-based access in our REST APIs. I resolved this by incorporating JWT for secure token management, ensuring that only authorized users could access sensitive data. These solutions significantly improved the application''s performance and security.', 43, false, '{"note": "The candidate provided a detailed and relevant answer with specific examples of challenges and solutions.", "relevance": 95, "needsFollowUp": false, "missingConcepts": [], "followUpQuestion": ""}', '2026-10-01 06:50:31', NULL, false, 'Certainly! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, one major challenge was optimizing MongoDB query performance, as the application handled around 120,000 users monthly. Initial queries were slow, affecting user experience. To tackle this, I implemented compound indexes and utilized aggregation pipelines, which reduced query times by 60%. Additionally, I faced challenges with role-based access in our REST APIs. I resolved this by incorporating JWT for secure token management, ensuring that only authorized users could access sensitive data. These solutions significantly improved the application''s performance and security.', 'Certainly! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, one major challenge was optimizing MongoDB query performance, as the application handled around 120,000 users monthly. Initial queries were slow, affecting user experience. To tackle this, I implemented compound indexes and utilized aggregation pipelines, which reduced query times by 60%. Additionally, I faced challenges with role-based access in our REST APIs. I resolved this by incorporating JWT for secure token management, ensuring that only authorized users could access sensitive data. These solutions significantly improved the application''s performance and security.', 0.94);
INSERT INTO public.interview_answers (id, "questionId", transcript, "durationSeconds", "timedOut", evaluation, "answeredAt", "correctedTranscript", "manuallyCorrected", "normalizedTranscript", "rawTranscript", "sttConfidence") VALUES ('cmuwf67bc00d9wxxm6ej831oi', 'cmuwf62m000d7wxxmoh6j7z9b', 'To secure a Node.js REST API handling customer financial data, I would implement several key measures. First, I would use JWT for authentication, ensuring that only authorized users can access sensitive endpoints. I would also enforce role-based access control to restrict permissions based on user roles. Additionally, I''d validate all incoming data to prevent injection attacks and employ HTTPS to encrypt data in transit. To further enhance security, I would set up rate limiting to prevent abuse and use logging to monitor access patterns. In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I designed REST APIs with these security practices, which helped build a loan-application portal that is secure and compliant for over 120,000 users monthly.', 54, false, '{"note": "Candidate provided a solid overview but could expand on role-based access control implementation.", "relevance": 90, "needsFollowUp": false, "missingConcepts": [], "followUpQuestion": "Can you elaborate on how you would implement role-based access control in this context?"}', '2026-10-01 06:51:39', NULL, false, 'To secure a Node.js REST API handling customer financial data, I would implement several key measures. First, I would use JWT for authentication, ensuring that only authorized users can access sensitive endpoints. I would also enforce role-based access control to restrict permissions based on user roles. Additionally, I''d validate all incoming data to prevent injection attacks and employ HTTPS to encrypt data in transit. To further enhance security, I would set up rate limiting to prevent abuse and use logging to monitor access patterns. In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I designed REST APIs with these security practices, which helped build a loan-application portal that is secure and compliant for over 120,000 users monthly.', 'To secure a Node.js REST API handling customer financial data, I would implement several key measures. First, I would use JWT for authentication, ensuring that only authorized users can access sensitive endpoints. I would also enforce role-based access control to restrict permissions based on user roles. Additionally, I''d validate all incoming data to prevent injection attacks and employ HTTPS to encrypt data in transit. To further enhance security, I would set up rate limiting to prevent abuse and use logging to monitor access patterns. In my current role at PayNest Technologies, I designed REST APIs with these security practices, which helped build a loan-application portal that is secure and compliant for over 120,000 users monthly.', 0.94);
INSERT INTO public.interview_answers (id, "questionId", transcript, "durationSeconds", "timedOut", evaluation, "answeredAt", "correctedTranscript", "manuallyCorrected", "normalizedTranscript", "rawTranscript", "sttConfidence") VALUES ('cmuwf6dk400ddwxxmsthpczv1', 'cmuwf69f500dbwxxmasf909ob', 'Absolutely! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, we faced a challenge with performance and security. We needed to implement JWT for user authentication, which is great for security but can slow down API response times if not managed properly. 

To optimize this, I decided to implement JWT refresh tokens for maintaining user sessions without requiring them to log in repeatedly. This choice significantly enhanced user experience while still ensuring secure access. Additionally, I focused on reducing MongoDB query times by 60% using compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This trade-off between security and performance ensured our portal could handle 120,000 customers a month efficiently without compromising on security features.', 52, false, '{"note": "Candidate provided a strong example with clear trade-offs and decisions made.", "relevance": 95, "needsFollowUp": false, "missingConcepts": [], "followUpQuestion": ""}', '2026-10-01 06:52:52', NULL, false, 'Absolutely! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, we faced a challenge with performance and security. We needed to implement JWT for user authentication, which is great for security but can slow down API response times if not managed properly. To optimize this, I decided to implement JWT refresh tokens for maintaining user sessions without requiring them to log in repeatedly. This choice significantly enhanced user experience while still ensuring secure access. Additionally, I focused on reducing MongoDB query times by 60% using compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This trade-off between security and performance ensured our portal could handle 120,000 customers a month efficiently without compromising on security features.', 'Absolutely! While working on the loan-application portal at PayNest Technologies, we faced a challenge with performance and security. We needed to implement JWT for user authentication, which is great for security but can slow down API response times if not managed properly. 

To optimize this, I decided to implement JWT refresh tokens for maintaining user sessions without requiring them to log in repeatedly. This choice significantly enhanced user experience while still ensuring secure access. Additionally, I focused on reducing MongoDB query times by 60% using compound indexes and aggregation pipelines. This trade-off between security and performance ensured our portal could handle 120,000 customers a month efficiently without compromising on security features.', 0.94);
